  "stateMatrixCompleteness": "High and regular. Every form control has size 1-3 (Button 1-4) x variants (Button: classic|solid|soft|surface|outline|ghost; TextField/TextArea/Select/Slider/Switch/Radio: classic|surface|soft; Card: surface|classic|ghost sizes 1-5; Badge: solid|soft|surface|outline sizes 1-3; Callout soft|surface|outline; Table surface|ghost; Avatar solid|soft sizes 1-9; Kbd classic|soft) x color (any of 26 accents) x highContrast boolean x radius override. States per variant: default/hover/active/focus-visible/disabled/loading (Button loading prop). Responsive size props via breakpoints."
 },
 "tokenArchitecture": "Three layers. (1) Raw scales: --{colour}-1..12 and --{colour}-a1..a12 per hue (31 hues incl. grays), light on :root/.light, dark on .dark. (2) Role aliases: --accent-*, --gray-*, --focus-*, --color-background/panel/surface/overlay, remapped by data-accent-color / data-gray-color attributes on any element (nested Theme works). (3) Scale tokens: --space-1..9, --font-size-1..9, --line-height-1..9, --letter-spacing-1..9, --radius-1..6, --shadow-1..6, --cursor-*, all multiplied by --scaling and --radius-factor; components consume only layer 2-3. Naming is numeric (steps), never semantic words like 'primary'.",
 "distinctiveness": "The 12-step functional scale (each step has a fixed job) plus a single accent/gray/radius/scaling configuration surface. Hairline-shadow borders, tinted grays and soft p3 colours give a recognisable 'Radix' softness; text is system-font by default so identity comes from colour/radius only.",
 "weaknesses": [
  "Typography has no display face or personality; heading = text scale at bold",
  "Very tokenised numeric naming (blue-9) is not self-describing",
  "Default look is widely seen (generic SaaS-soft)",
  "Docs list step 7/8 roles inconsistently",
  "Docs warn Radix Colors are not meant to be customised, so brand hues need a parallel custom scale",
  "Motion is inline per component, no shared duration tokens",
  "Translucent panel default needs blur support and can reduce contrast"
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "Give every colour step a fixed job (bg/hover/active/border/solid/text) so components stay coloured with zero per-component decisions",
  "Expose few knobs (accent, gray, radius, scaling, panel) and derive everything from them via multipliers",
  "Pair each accent with a tinted gray of the nearest hue; allow pure gray as the neutral option",
  "Guarantee contrast by construction (step 11 = Lc 60, step 12 = Lc 90 on step 2)",
  "Define alpha variants for every step so overlays and borders adapt to any background",
  "Components pick radius by size step with max(radius-N, radius-full) so one switch changes shape language",
  "Ship the exact on-solid text colour per hue (white vs dark) as a token"
 ]
}